#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105905 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105561 :question/id #uuid "b41b2354-c339-5398-ab43-5886b8447c1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3294" :question/problem "Rounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$\n\n![](images/bc/bc9f32a9c0e8b042498a72e808a29274bd505e786d8ec43d0e0bc9888fdf6e44.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle ADC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/ac/acd2e923a65d0821cd59ed8b8274ceb5fc38def896467e37c8b1d454f958699e.png)\n\n First, we find the area for $\\triangle ABC,$ and get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & =\\frac{1}{2}(42)(35)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{36}^{∘} \\\\  & =735\\operatorname{sin}⁡{36}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈432.022\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $\\triangle ADC,$ and get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ADC} & =\\frac{1}{2}(20)(18)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘} \\\\  & =180\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈177.265\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD.$ We get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABC}+{A}_{ADC} \\\\  & =432.022+177.265 \\\\  & ≈609\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $609.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eba9db1e-481a-550a-a4de-52afa48eed8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102399} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0dc7a0-7c14-54e6-8360-6f151cbe56b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102400} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9cb464-a012-5b31-ac3b-939e2fc9c922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102401} {:answer/id #uuid "6a700756-913d-5595-b66e-0a5bc1b04cae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102402} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0cd577-3c04-54d4-8282-413c61911c3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102403}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ba670955-c6ce-564e-983f-2051680718f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102398}] :question/id #uuid "0dab1268-d1c2-5547-a6e5-c75f85a4f239" :question/math-academy-id "q-18180" :question/problem "![](images/98/98d0c5dfe759f744b361fe384c4c11c78e58ed6194086053b44076567081e986.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106439 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5668382-1e6c-5ada-8f6f-792ffd26ef91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104783} {:answer/id #uuid "e59316d1-4367-5461-a171-2a39cfa2466a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104784} {:answer/id #uuid "f212af3d-14ce-5430-8e0d-ebf2c473beac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104785} {:answer/id #uuid "358fdfcf-9dc7-5768-b6ee-2fbdf0a6a7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "47.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104786} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7a3aa7-b0f9-5de4-b78a-8ca8b6f7052f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104787}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9e80d5c1-4641-5da9-a2bc-641c532e791f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104782}] :question/id #uuid "419a42dc-188f-5378-85e0-27d5bb64db37" :question/math-academy-id "q-54258" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cc23cf5b5df6c51aac404c9e6a95ba3cfbdb2279bcd3dea11c6d56966d91a8dd.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234325 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a33798d-52c0-57f6-a233-6585edd299f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-72754" :question/problem "![](images/38/38e096b8d57404135b7fe3244e50989e66021f94bb2275c56956d8663575b4f8.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}{85}^{∘} \\\\  & =24\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}{85}^{∘} \\\\  & \\approx 23.908\\,7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 14\\cdot 16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}{37}^{∘} \\\\  & =112\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}{37}^{∘} \\\\  & \\approx 67.403\\,3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =23.908\\,7+67.403\\,3 \\\\  & =91.311\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $91.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6cee6b4-2a3f-5b80-8f79-bbdc774e729c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6cee6b4-2a3f-5b80-8f79-bbdc774e729c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293590} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0a67366-7358-5ccd-9b0a-b78d1e7fee7b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294715}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e17900e-d26f-58a6-baab-ca3dab29afb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-279762" :question/problem "![](images/54/54265327c77bedb300fe0d1f1f08ca3ab2d7ae37f35f49007d3f20ab3a21dbaa.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/b1/b1d0cf7c5a7c6ad7f0f52c8686239920fabcb05be57372ae0c7c9c9491838a52.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈25.981,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 25.981 \\\\  & =51.962.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $52.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45026583-2f3c-517d-8eb5-a28f4404f1e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45026583-2f3c-517d-8eb5-a28f4404f1e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295658} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0829f4e-98e2-572d-86bc-74f61d3d7503" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297067}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3bb44f47-acad-5cce-bb2a-a2f32b8da827" :question/math-academy-id "q-285703" :question/problem "![](images/da/dafaf2421aaa9be80c472b4dde7c941defb94f7f3533fda4ebb2fdcee2b60e31.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/cd/cd9363a3cc686ae45f49c982f4b31ad75b7c7897dcf7e8af58e530dba6946e1d.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & =21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈19.096\\,0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9+19.096\\,0 \\\\  & ≈35.182\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $35.2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d4ed0c9-7f6f-5206-af74-9b5a71b8bb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d4ed0c9-7f6f-5206-af74-9b5a71b8bb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295871} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa377d1-aa1d-58ff-8f43-f26275cc3530" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297031}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8934630b-77d1-55ee-b8d1-51a8be5db47e" :question/math-academy-id "q-285737" :question/problem "![](images/48/48dec69962b09e9c189de23c398db63066b6da8d62a04f1cd01fdc9f333f899f.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/d6/d6a654d3154ba8af8fc4f7654e62c6bacfede7017322aeed21a143e2634dcd14.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈13.856,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 13.856 \\\\  & =27.712.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $28.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da74ef9-bc35-5bd4-a775-6227e3770b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330069} {:answer/id #uuid "4cab3170-0757-5382-a642-6a610aa18961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330646} {:answer/id #uuid "51dae920-7e93-5d91-8ef7-09f5119e363c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330692} {:answer/id #uuid "af914ae5-dadd-5a35-bda2-56290cd884a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331501} {:answer/id #uuid "e18ffbce-0f6c-59ce-84c9-1967feb16d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0da74ef9-bc35-5bd4-a775-6227e3770b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330069} :answer-field/id #uuid "489b8504-24f4-5803-ae22-0dec31049edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332322}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a963f45-1ffb-5d74-b38f-c635a0c24c20" :question/math-academy-id "q-54339" :question/problem "![](images/f1/f1ae263b71fa17fd648464c24b307c064c9e657c2c9f6b36faf8c9819f1fb285.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/a6/a60b049aef53aef28802b084b3e445fd6253978500ca981d3b799977523cdd71.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(8)(5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.383,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 16.383 \\\\  & =32.766.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $33.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03142fcd-6f19-5692-a3da-da502772ac2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333014} {:answer/id #uuid "0430ddd0-499d-53c2-994f-613bdc887648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333022} {:answer/id #uuid "454df806-b05f-5668-bfc1-d7cfdc549af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333630} {:answer/id #uuid "a5074c1a-1d5f-5090-b302-4eafa6e852a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334436} {:answer/id #uuid "d012d020-5f8d-544e-8a7f-5e3267236519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "69.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "454df806-b05f-5668-bfc1-d7cfdc549af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333630} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe2925de-ca80-5513-860d-a4f360e0060a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335683}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbe5d0e1-3ef1-5eeb-b6da-bb45b64850c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-67787" :question/problem "![](images/48/488389632139d269e24958275ee20a9e5f8582fd0966e4d935487d238a463180.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/68/68f5708d49577befe9bac6a7aaf6a54fcdb30dcd344367d2c69b8924093dbb61.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 14\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & =84\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈56.315\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =17.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.994\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =56.315\\,8+16.994\\,8 \\\\  & =73.310\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $73.3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335940 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018db6be-c2e0-5b71-a965-9b8b09b6b735" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "416" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333001} {:answer/id #uuid "0d660a41-028d-58ab-aa41-4492c238acc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "462" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333106} {:answer/id #uuid "30e73ae1-8ede-5d25-9355-5c9e2abec14c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "458" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333440} {:answer/id #uuid "b829245a-508c-5df4-ab92-1586e59a733f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "437" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334602} {:answer/id #uuid "ec58f96d-7f07-5f65-a5c3-6ba3c108fcad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "422" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30e73ae1-8ede-5d25-9355-5c9e2abec14c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "458" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333440} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fd4a639-ac17-50f3-9f71-1f9152848f0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335392}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd32da9e-3e34-5cd6-ac25-c9a996a26523" :question/math-academy-id "q-67788" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0b100942a658966a5feea8a8677e7cfe86f21970a443385ff06034bbcb3d497.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ACD$ and $△ABC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/7e/7e3232258a523e4dbfebb6c380f5b88c2a54036b4d719e70ebf9060054f825d7.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ACD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 18\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =189\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈163.679,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△ABC:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 36\\cdot 30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘} \\\\  & =540\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈294.105,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ACD}+{A}_{ABC} \\\\  & =163.679+294.105 \\\\  & =457.784\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $458.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d011d15-855e-593b-a305-503c6f4d7b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339829} {:answer/id #uuid "5049855a-0cf1-52ff-a6d7-82ad580a1998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339858} {:answer/id #uuid "65970e9b-6b55-55f9-87cb-642a2bfcf59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "132" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340026} {:answer/id #uuid "810e57dc-6211-51e2-9530-7c30c274a5a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340286} {:answer/id #uuid "941f7586-f901-520c-ba5a-d3f77fa4895c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5049855a-0cf1-52ff-a6d7-82ad580a1998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339858} :answer-field/id #uuid "59a7e60a-6a2a-50ed-b8ee-1ebc1c309e07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341540}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1e965d5-3d0b-5c28-9671-3eb1e1598d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72768" :question/problem "![](images/36/36af7324fd2112d94feddc5a1a02a91d97bbc0866cb93a6ca711dd73f566305a.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/7c/7cfcb5cdf77b4afbf25afd64e37bb33f0ab2c211e09659181bfc16db0ccd2db7.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(18)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =72\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈67.658,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 67.658 \\\\  & =135.316.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $135.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105906 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105562 :question/id #uuid "472216c8-da7d-58fb-9056-e71d5e33460d" :question/math-academy-id "e-3297" :question/problem "The area of $ABCD$ is $300\\, \\text{cm}^2.$  What is the area of $\\triangle ABC$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n![](images/c0/c06ffb123bdd24c3f83419767b6d1578223b8093089b79f91aae8f1fc6121305.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $\\triangle ACD.$ We get \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot DA\\cdot DC\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(25)(32)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =400\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =375.877... \\\\  & ≈376\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ and $\\triangle ACD$ gives the area of $\\triangle ABC.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & ={A}_{ACD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =376-300 \\\\  & =76\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106088 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79e7cd07-add5-5d10-80df-71a143f0f74a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285917} {:answer/id #uuid "7ae3971d-6093-5438-8c3a-22800ae8c4ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285923} {:answer/id #uuid "af0e1058-b843-5261-b5a1-91f185eb6d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286384} {:answer/id #uuid "cf53b765-2868-582d-9cd7-9346da7219c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286672} {:answer/id #uuid "fec4ef30-225b-5860-99b0-932b04fb666f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af0e1058-b843-5261-b5a1-91f185eb6d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286384} :answer-field/id #uuid "874f169b-33d9-5860-93b7-c25e52780651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287433}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "157038e6-e68d-5ec0-b464-27301542d833" :question/math-academy-id "q-18188" :question/problem "![](images/98/98b3193783f0ac19bcb78035b133ad8dbf956528dfb7474606cc586d3bfecc34.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $90{\\text{ in}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =168\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =139.278… \\\\  & ≈139{\\text{ in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =139-90 \\\\  & =49{\\text{ in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068aef71-9d0b-5bf0-a059-3345c4a26cd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102411} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0ff031-ddc9-58a4-b121-fc07f61ea402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102412} {:answer/id #uuid "201fdfed-a087-5b36-9b41-dbae66a732df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102413} {:answer/id #uuid "28111f42-ee7e-5125-a586-64005136f60c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102414} {:answer/id #uuid "77ca9711-f760-5ed4-9e2e-cc5dae5c27ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102415}] :answer-field/id #uuid "60055fce-3ff2-5b37-83d6-d6b9c5982646" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102410}] :question/id #uuid "76bfb6f5-5246-5d99-87f0-2edbbb96b1d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-18192" :question/problem "![](images/38/38004f5c93b047155973d32caa632c2c506d526c09ea891a7a02864997860f0e.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $15in^{2}$. What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de0df21-0a88-5163-a683-4cb2c599085d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 175921862