=23-17 \\\\  & =6{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f1e9b2-0fc8-53a9-bc65-f1cb3d45dfc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85f1e9b2-0fc8-53a9-bc65-f1cb3d45dfc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295985} :answer-field/id #uuid "16b8a569-d89d-5ee2-ba68-fe0246dbd470" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296678}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1777d556-717d-5159-9602-61018070f640" :question/math-academy-id "q-285740" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b69082ef86283bc842ce487b62901e8946ffff53ab8323a6fc846f68c5869aae.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $10{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{cm}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =11.591… \\\\  & ≈12{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "463216f3-e0fc-54f6-a6cb-048b38856ff0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "463216f3-e0fc-54f6-a6cb-048b38856ff0" 