9cad-7ab2dae7694f" :question/math-academy-id "q-285769" :question/problem "![](images/33/33aff6da54b72146f89bbd580a889a4050bff89bca86ddb6b74b80f62875a470.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $5{\\text{ km}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{km}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2.5\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =6.682… \\\\  & ≈7{\\text{ km}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =2{\\text{ km}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf942b6a-2bda-5195-bed6-c7db43c5e112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf942b6a-2bda-5195-bed6-c7db43c5e112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296279} :answer-field/id #uuid "dec8dded-fc4f-5c4b-9bb5-dd783b604c0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297095}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ed8b4aa-f539-5288-91e4-4588aa44c54e" :question/math-academy-id "q-285786" :question/problem "![](images/af/aff2ca3dac212832eb3b2219678dab3f4029319ce6b09f8c134f9dcc99b72640.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $13{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 6.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16{\\text{ mi}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =16-13 \\\\  & =3{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f07a6b5-32ea-529d-9160-238820145dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339267} {:answer/id #uuid "174b9032-2956-564a-826e-c2c81592003e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339336} {:answer/id #uuid "508acfdf-0761-5691-be12-cc8ecd53beb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339862} {:answer/id #uuid "84059e1d-50ea-57c1-a02c-e73cba67744f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340317} {:answer/id #uuid "f79db4a6-d5f5-5ae3-9697-f4ab3f3df76c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "508acfdf-0761-5691-be12-cc8ecd53beb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339862} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea1b3e9c-7be4-50dc-84b7-55a05c94254f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341796}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d86eb6a4-4303-50bf-b47a-fa898e3f8037" :question/math-academy-id "q-72764" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f53996727138b9442ac041cf492618db8287b54ba652c4f9e375cdde27dc1862.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{52}^{∘} \\\\  & =67.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{52}^{∘} \\\\  & =53.190… \\\\  & ≈53{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =53-34 \\\\  & =19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105596 :question/id #uuid "b3be2b13-b455-5dde-accf-259c075e1e1f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4350" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "842559ea-e8de-579e-b0e2-e4bc6fd93411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104003} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b8cf03-23cd-55b9-a44e-0a91507aef2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104004} {:answer/id #uuid "07566dee-dcab-5b2b-aeff-bb244caaef53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104005} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf80ba1-1722-5eda-8a01-2202aeb56d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104006} {:answer/id #uuid "78cee756-b381-5b9c-8874-9a1d39a5f075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104007}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fe2fd0b9-0fb1-5157-8647-5b6a0eebb344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104002}] :question/id #uuid "51de3e44-6cdb-5f9b-ba39-3a79c7ef7ab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-40214" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $x = ⟨3, 5, 0⟩$, $y = ⟨3, 2, 0⟩$ and $z = ⟨3, 4, 5⟩$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "268ade47-b758-5c24-b7aa-22cfb3ca64e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "79" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104009} {:answer/id #uuid "33efc085-6fcb-5388-bfd0-44fc6e3e74ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104010} {:answer/id #uuid "3613c7b9-5056-515a-a447-1260f03958c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104011} {:answer/id #uuid "5c78f5d1-616c-594d-9347-a9241